# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PaddleOCR / PaddleX model artifacts and caches
#
# Models are downloaded on first run and vendored into /models for deployment.
# They are large binaries and must never be committed.
#
# Leading slash is required — an unanchored "models/" would also swallow
# app/models/, which holds the Pydantic request/response models.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/models/
.paddleocr/
.paddlex/
paddlex/
*.pdmodel
*.pdiparams
*.pdiparams.info
*.pdopt
*.nb
inference/
inference_results/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime output — scan images, debug artifacts, logs
#
# Scan images are operational data, not source. Paths come from config.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
images/
processed/
debug/
logs/
*.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sample data
#
# Directory structure and ground-truth JSON ARE tracked.
# The image binaries are NOT — they are large and carry real product data.
# Captures are taken on the TC22 through the app's own sample mode; there is
# no download step and no public dataset (CLAUDE.md section 25).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
sample_data/**/*.jpg
sample_data/**/*.jpeg
sample_data/**/*.png
sample_data/**/*.bmp
sample_data/**/*.tif
sample_data/**/*.tiff
sample_data/**/*.webp
sample_data/**/*.zip
sample_data/**/*.tar.gz
!sample_data/**/.gitkeep
!sample_data/**/README.md

# Downloaded third-party datasets
datasets/

